The loss of 3 cans of paint resulted in 5 fewer rooms being painted, so the ratio of cans of paint to rooms painted is $3: 5$. Hence for 25 rooms she would require $\dfrac{3}{5} \cdot 25=15$ cans of paint.

\section*{OR}

If she used $x$ cans of paint for 25 rooms, then $\dfrac{x+3}{30}=\dfrac{x}{25}$. Hence $25 x+75=30 x$, and $\boxed{x=15}$.

